    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved all date-derived owner values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the calendar year in which it ends \u2014 e.g. 1 July 2026 \u2192 `FY27`, 15 June 2026 \u2192 `FY26`). The fiscal year is derived from the already business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` stored on the owner.\n\n### `src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`\n- **Added `getFiscalYear()`** returning `FY<YY>` (two-digit fiscal year) from the registration date, plus a private `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` helper (`month >= 7 ? year+1 : year`).\n- **`getMembershipNumber()`** \u2014 the `-M<YY>` year segment now uses the fiscal year instead of the calendar year of the registration date.\n- **Replaced `getTenureDays()` with `getTenureFiscalYears()`** \u2014 tenure is now the number of elapsed fiscal-year boundaries between the registration date and today, rather than a 365-day count.\n- **`getMembershipPoints()`** \u2014 the 3 tenure points are now awarded when tenure spans \u2265 1 elapsed fiscal year (a newly created owner still has zero tenure, so the invariant that points aren't awarded at create time is preserved). Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n### `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`\n- Added the read-only `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps `getFiscalYear()`).\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe test suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), and the audit log confirms the new behaviour end-to-end: an owner rolled to a registration date of `2026-10-05` gets `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` (October \u2192 FY27), and `coreReturnsFiscalYear` sees a well-formed `FY27`.",
